* There was a "standing invite" to Libertarians to move to Ft. Collins, CO
  a while back. As far as I know it had no big effect.

* Keep an eye on Montana in 1995. There is a secession referendum planned.
  "Moving to Montana soon ..."

* Several states, CO among them, are considering or have had proposed, 10th
  amendment enforcement resolutions calling on the U.S. Gummint to stop
  enacting mandates and acting outside its powers. 

I don't know how far any of these things will get, but it's exciting to see
them seriously proposed. Bear in mind that the USA refrained from trying
Jefferson Davis for treason exactly because his defense would have been that 
secession was perfectly legal, there being nothing in the Constitution to
limit it, and an explicit guarantee in the BoR that all powers not granted
to the US were reserved by the states or the people.



 
